I'm not sure about all of the possible reasons for level draining creatures
as a whole, but wraiths, in particular are nice in that if you eat a wraith
corpse it has the same effect as a potion of gain level ( except of course
that it is possible to choke to death on a dead wraith, and they don't
boil and explode if you're hit by a bolt of fire... )

As to other reasons, I think there may be something to do with the way you
lose hit points and experience when 'drained' as compared to how you gain them
( it may be a little one sided ( ie: you gain more than you lose )) but this
is semi-speculation at this point, I'm sure others will expand if asked...




